# .git-arch-identities — correct contributor identity merges/splits the
# heuristic can't safely infer on its own. Copy this to `.git-arch-identities`
# in your repo root and edit. Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# merge: group several emails belonging to ONE person into a single identity.
#   Use this when one contributor commits under multiple emails the tool can't
#   link (e.g. a personal address and a work address with different local-parts).
# merge: alice@personal.com, alice@work.com, 12345+alice@users.noreply.github.com
#
# split: force an email to stay SEPARATE from any heuristic merge.
#   Use this for a shared account (e.g. a release/CI mailbox) that the tool
#   might otherwise fold into a person.
# split: ci-shared@example.com
